{"timestamp":"2026-05-19T17:55:36.996Z","type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"agent_message","message":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"Fallback logging keeps the wrong global session id\",\"category\":\"bug\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\",\"startLine\":121,\"endLine\":132,\"symbol\":\"Init\",\"quote\":\"logger = createLogger(os.Stderr, level)\\n\\t\\t\\treturn nil\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\",\"startLine\":135,\"endLine\":138,\"symbol\":\"Init\",\"quote\":\"currentSessionID = sessionID\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go\",\"startLine\":222,\"endLine\":248,\"symbol\":\"TestInit_FallsBackToStderrOnError\",\"quote\":null}],\"reasoning\":\"Init documents that a non-empty sessionID is stored on every log line, but currentSessionID is only assigned on the successful file-backed path. If creating the log directory or opening entire.log fails, Init returns a working stderr logger with either an empty session_id on first initialization or a stale session_id from a previous Init. That makes fallback logs unfilterable or misattributed exactly when diagnostics are needed most.\",\"reproduction\":\"Call Init(ctx, \\\"old-session\\\") successfully, then arrange .entire/logs/entire.log to be a directory and call Init(ctx, \\\"new-session\\\"). A subsequent Info(ctx, ...) logs through stderr with currentSessionID still set to \\\"old-session\\\".\",\"recommendation\":\"Assign currentSessionID = sessionID before any fallback return after validation, or use a small helper that installs logger/currentSessionID together for both stderr and file-backed loggers.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"TestInit_FallsBackToStderrOnError only checks that Init returns nil and Info does not panic; it does not capture stderr or assert the session_id field on fallback output.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Extend TestInit_FallsBackToStderrOnError to initialize one session successfully,