sBackToStderrOnError to initialize one session successfully, force the fallback path with a different session ID, capture stderr, and assert the emitted JSON contains the new session_id and not the old one.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go Init fallback branches plus logger fallback coverage in cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go\"},{\"title\":\"Close leaves logger pointing at a closed buffered writer\",\"category\":\"data-loss\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\",\"startLine\":135,\"endLine\":138,\"symbol\":\"Init\",\"quote\":\"logBufWriter = bufio.NewWriterSize(f, 8192)\\n\\tlogger = createLogger(logBufWriter, level)\"},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\",\"startLine\":146,\"endLine\":159,\"symbol\":\"Close\",\"quote\":null},{\"path\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\",\"startLine\":264,\"endLine\":289,\"symbol\":\"log\",\"quote\":\"if l == nil {\\n\\t\\tl = slog.Default()\\n\\t}\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Close flushes and closes logBufWriter/logFile and nils those globals, but it does not clear logger. The slog handler created in Init still owns the old bufio.Writer, so any logging after Close uses a handler backed by a closed file instead of falling back to slog.Default. Because the package-level log functions do not return write errors, those post-Close log records are silently dropped.\",\"reproduction\":\"Call Init(ctx, \\\"session\\\"), then Close(), then Info(context.Background(), \\\"after close\\\"). The logger global is still non-nil, so log uses the stale handler rather than slog.Default; the record is not written to the file and no error is surfaced.\",\"recommendation\":\"Set logger = nil in Close after closing the file, or replace it with a stderr/default logger if post-Close logging should remain explicitly supported. Add a regression test that logs after Close and verifies it goes to the expected fallback sink instead of the closed file-backed handler.\",\"whyTestsDoNotAlreadyCoverThis\":\"TestClose_SafeToCallMultipleTimes only verifies that repeated Close calls do not panic; it never emits a log after Close or checks that the logger state no longer references the closed writer.\",\"suggestedRegressionTest\":\"Add a test that installs a file-backed logger, closes it, then logs again with a captured default/stderr logger or reinitialization expectation, asserting the post-Close record is not silently lost through the closed bufio.Writer.\",\"minimumFixScope\":\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go Close state reset plus one logger_test.go post-Close behavior test\"}],\"inspected\":{\"files\":[\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/context.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/context_test.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/logging/logger_test.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/agent/types/agent.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/paths/paths.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/paths/transcript.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/paths/worktree.go\",\"cmd/entire/cli/validation/validators.go\"],\"symbols\":[\"WithSession\",\"WithParentSession\",\"WithToolCall\",\"WithComponent\",\"WithAgent\",\"SessionIDFromContext\",\"ParentSessionIDFromContext\",\"ToolCallIDFromContext\",\"ComponentFromContext\",\"AgentFromContext\",\"Init\",\"Close\",\"resetLogger\",\"createLogger\",\"parseLogLevel\",\"isValidLogLevel\",\"Debug\",\"Info\",\"Warn\",\"Error\",\"LogDuration\",\"log\",\"attrsFromContext\",\"ValidateSessionID\",\"WorktreeRoot\"],\"notes\":[\"Reviewed the owned logging package files and the linked tests as evidence of intended behavior.\",\"Did not run the full test suite; this was a source review of the supplied feature scope.\"]}}","completed_at":1779213338,"duration_ms":153874,"time_to_first_token_ms":40900}}
